{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system","id":20503,"title":"Has anyone done work on divorcing the various aspects of the Tier system?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-29T21:53:23-08:00","id":20503,"title":"Has anyone done work on divorcing the various aspects of the Tier system?","content":"I think I started a thread on this in the old forum just in time for the switch over. Anyways.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in divorcing the current Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy structure. We have the GMC defining Tier as geographic scale of the threat, while H:tV has Tier as a funny combination of size, power level, and organization. As it stands, only Tier 3 groups gain access to Endowments, but the rest of the system falls apart when you compare the size of the Lucifuge (666 members; Tier 3) to that of, say, The Union (cells all across the United States; Tier 2). <br /> <br /> I was reading King's Raven's work on his Cults books (fantastic stuff, by the way) and he has a number of Merits that resemble Endowments, but with no required Conspiracy. The idea of playing Endowed hunters, sans Conspiracy, sounds nice, as does the idea of a Tier 3 organization without access to magic or super-science (I'm bad at writing Endowments, but prefer Tier 3 groups).<br /> <br /> This is a bit of a rambling post, but I was just curious about it all. What would you break Tier up into?<br /> <br /> You could easily say:<ul><li>Size of the Hunter organization: (Tiers 2 and 3)</li> <li>Power of the Hunter organization: (Tiers 1 through 3)</li> <li>Scale of the threat: (Tiers 1 through 4)</li> <li>Power of the threat: (Tiers 1 through 4)</li> </ul>Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T00:38:31-08:00","id":20534,"title":"","content":"There's a partly done section on this in chapter 5, I'm not sure you've gotten that far yet? I go for the size of the organisation, how much control it exerts over it's members, the scope of the story, and access to endowments: Size, Organisation, Scope, Mojo. IMO organisation is the most important one since that's the one that really defines how you roleplay the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-30-2013, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T01:01:50-08:00","id":20543,"title":"","content":"Rats, I hadn't hit that chapter yet and you've done both my exploding of Tier into multiple categories AND the Mummy response team idea! Great minds, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I feel like your guidelines, when combined with the scale aspect of Tier in the GMC and perhaps some sort of Tier for the enemy as well. You could be a small, loosely-controlled group (Tier 1 or 2 for Size, Organization, and Control) with access to magic (Tier 2 or 3 Mojo) in one city (Tier 2), dealing with an apocalyptic cult (a Tier 2 group attempting to cause a Tier 4 problem). Bah, I'm not making sense anymore.<br /> <br /> I'll slave over it and post some notes soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T07:34:52-08:00","id":23140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>atamajakki:</b><br /> I'm interested in divorcing the current Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy structure. We have the GMC defining Tier as geographic scale of the threat, while H:tV has Tier as a funny combination of size, power level, and organization. </div> </div> </div>Tiers mean slightly different things in different gamelines; for Hunter, it's best thought of as how far away from the normal human world you've gone in order to fight the darkness.<br /> <br /> So organisations of the like-minded, with a consequential philosophy of what the hunt means, is the tipping point between tier 1 and above - while tier 3 is marked by the use of supernatural tools, or membership in a group where hunting becomes your actual job (and thus your job becomes a tie the supernatural world, not the human one) - the Lucifuge, where their supernature is in their blood and the Vigil can never be escaped, are the closest to what would be Hunter's tier 4.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T07:55:35-08:00","id":23149,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree Sunless. That just doesn't match up to what the Tiers the orgs are. Ashwood Abbey, while perhaps not full timers, have gone further from normal humanity than Task Force: Valkyrie.<br /> <br /> The overall power of the organisation is the closest thing to the meaning of Tier (and it's still the one I think works best with Hunter's themes) but even that's inconsistent. This is why I feel it's worth having a deconstruction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now here's where I will agree with you. As one factor among many distance form the normal world is a great way to look at climbing the tiers. I'm going to add that to cults with Tier 4 being an actual chuthulu cultist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T07:35:18-08:00","id":25094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to disagree Sunless. That just doesn't match up to what the Tiers the orgs are. Ashwood Abbey, while perhaps not full timers, have gone further from normal humanity than Task Force: Valkyrie. </div> </div> </div>No, they've become less <i>humane</i>. But they still have a life outside the Vigil to a greater extent than someone whose actual job is monster-hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T07:40:24-08:00","id":25097,"title":"","content":"But surely how humane you are is the important metric. It's a lot more thematic and impactful than whether you have a full time job or not.<br /> <br /> [edit]On second thought though; I would add that the Ascending Ones often have full time non-vigil jobs. The only accurate statement for how Hunter actually used Tiers was &quot;Endowment, yes or no?&quot; and they broke that rule as early as Witchfinders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-08-2013, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T05:59:14-08:00","id":25754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But surely how humane you are is the important metric. </div> </div> </div>Not for tier, no. Certainly not as much as ties to the world you're fighting for.<br /> <br /> (And while the Ascending Ones may have those, they've still warped their bodies with poisons to become able to use elixirs, and are members of a millennia-old secret society they don't get to quit)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only accurate statement for how Hunter actually used Tiers was &quot;Endowment, yes or no?&quot; and they broke that rule as early as Witchfinders. </div> </div> </div>Bent, not broke IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:53:50-08:00","id":25774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=25754#post25754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for tier, no. Certainly not as much as ties to the world you're fighting for.</div> </div> </div> </div> But most of the Conspiracies don't stop you having ties to the mortal world, all the time a Compact Hunter is spending on their money-making job a paid hunter could be spending socialising with their mundane friends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=25754#post25754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And while the Ascending Ones may have those, they've still warped their bodies with poisons to become able to use elixirs, and are members of a millennia-old secret society they don't get to quit)</div> </div> </div> </div> Which doesn't affect their ties to the word they're fighting for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=25754#post25754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bent, not broke IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say broke, The Promethian Brotherhood had a top tier Endowment by any metric but wordcount.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:24:43-08:00","id":27289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But most of the Conspiracies don't stop you having ties to the mortal world, all the time a Compact Hunter is spending on their money-making job a paid hunter could be spending socialising with their mundane friends. </div> </div> </div>Any hunter can choose the latter. It doesnt' change the fact that a hunter whose profession - the thing that mechanically stands as a representation of self-image - is part of the vigil has fewer ties than one whose profession is not. And a TFV job is more than &quot;paying&quot; - it's also one that even if you can quit, you're still going to be bound by most of its rules for the rest of your life.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which doesn't affect their ties to the word they're fighting for. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you've forgotten that I'm treating loss of ties to the human world as a <i>subset</i> of distance from it, not as an exact conflation - all the other things I mentioned are other subsets.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Promethian Brotherhood had a top tier Endowment by any metric but wordcount. </div> </div> </div>And its unreliability, and that the powers it offers are explicitly not theirs, are temporary, and are dependent on whom you've murdered recently, and can't be refined and developed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:36:17-08:00","id":27399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=27289#post27289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any hunter can choose the latter. It doesnt' change the fact that a hunter whose profession - the thing that mechanically stands as a representation of self-image - is part of the vigil has fewer ties than one whose profession is not. And a TFV job is more than &quot;paying&quot; - it's also one that even if you can quit, you're still going to be bound by most of its rules for the rest of your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point; I guess I don't feel that way because Hunter never sold me on the concept of your Profession being your tie to mundanity.<br /> <br /> TF:V turn over their employment to the Vigil. The Loyalists of Thule turn over their free time to the Vigil. Both are tightly bound by their organisations rules. If you don't give bonus points for Professions then I see those two as roughly equivalent. That's before you get to complications like the Null Mysteriis who's Profession is directly tied to their vigil but they don't get paid for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately, looking at Tiers as distance from humanity is a completely valid thing to do, more importantly it's an interesting thing to do. The only place I disagree with you, is that it accurately represents the current organisations. I think you would have to put Ashwood Abbey at Tier 3 - because how humane you are absolutely is a measure of how distant you are from the normal world - and VASCU at Tier 2. Some of the others might need adjusting too<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=27289#post27289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its unreliability, and that the powers it offers are explicitly not theirs, are temporary, and are dependent on whom you've murdered recently, and can't be refined and developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Endowment is the ability to steal Gnosis; not the Gnosis/Mysteries themselves.<br /> <br /> Those powers are theirs and explicitly can be refined and developed - they've been doing that for all their existence. If you need more evidence the upcoming Endowment Anthropophagy is practically <i>the exact same endowment</i> only targeting immortals instead of witches. It's given to a Conspiracy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:00:03-08:00","id":27436,"title":"","content":"Well, the Promethean Brotherhood are presented as a compact on the verge of being a conspiracy, right? So yeah, they had the Rite of Hecate since the beginning, but at first it hardly worked and it took allot of time to translate it and understand how it worked. You may say that their rise in power and influence (a.k.a, rising in the tiers) is also reflected in the improvement of the understanding and reliability of the Rite.<br /> <br /> In short, I don't really think that the Promethean Brotherhood is an example for a &quot;compact with supernatural powers&quot;, but are more an example for a &quot;2.5 tier group&quot;- meaning, a compact which is on the verge of becoming a conspiracy/ a conspiracy on the verge of breaking down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:18:10-08:00","id":27460,"title":"","content":"As you said though, they had the Rite from the beginning and while you are right that it was unreliable at the start there it does say that in the first six years, back when the rite was poorly understood, they had successfully stolen and kept gnosis for months or even years (curiously the mechanics say that's impossible). In fact, the very first time Jacob Hite performed the Rite it worked for a week.<br /> <br /> So while the Rite has imporved I don't think you can say that the rite alone has changed enough to move them up or down a Tier. It's the growth in membership, resources, etc that did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:47:00-08:00","id":27494,"title":"","content":"Well, I think it works on both ways. I mean, the Rite has given them a certain resources while the resources helped them to better understand the Rite. What I wanted to say (and forgot to add in my previous post) is that not any &quot;supernatural ability&quot; is an Endowment, IMO. I mean, just having a supernatural power is just having a supernatural power, which could be represented by a merit or something. A supernatural power (or equivalent, in case of TF:V, AKD and AO) turns into an Endowment once it is reliable, can be shared freely between the members of a certain organization and be used in number of ways (as represented with a 1-5 dots and the fact that there is more than one Relic, for example). Only once the Rite became reliable it could have been considered as a true Endowment, for only than it could do the same thing in the same way again and again and could be shared between the members of the Brotherhood. I think that the same is for the Lucifuge- there were always people with demonic blood in their veins. It is only after that Lady Lucifuge made her conspiracy that those powers were organized into the infernal rites of the Castigations instead of being wild demonic powers.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just how I interpret things :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T14:29:35-08:00","id":27534,"title":"","content":"Personally I say it's &quot;teachable&quot; rather than &quot;reliable&quot;. If you take the Gifted Merit from Witch Finders, that's reliable but isn't teachable. At least not easily, because if everyone could learn it one Gifted Hunter would quickly turn the entire Cell, then maybe the entire Compact Gifted. By this measure the Rite always was an Endowment, Jacob taught it to others, it just wasn't a very reliable Endowment. Anyway the book explicitly says the 1-5 Endowment applies to any point in the Compact's history (mind you, those rules also contradict the text hugely)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T15:39:08-08:00","id":27572,"title":"","content":"When I've said &quot;could be shared freely&quot; I meant to it as &quot;teachable&quot;, so I meant that in order for a merit to be considered as an Endowment it needs to be a) teachable b) reliable and c) 1-5 range. I also don't have an access to my Witchfinder book right now, so my to access to the exact mechanics of the Rite is limited to my memory. Anyway, like I said before, this is just my opinion, and it is based on how I understand the concept of what an &quot;Endowment&quot; is. The Rite always worked, but in order to it to become an Endowment the Brotherhood had to decipher the text and understand how it worked in more than &quot;you kill a witch and get her powers&quot;, so they could teach it to anyone who will join the compact. Again, it is just my opinion, and because there is no cannon explanation of what makes a merit into an Endowment (except of &quot;those are connected to a conspiracy and those are not&quot;), anyone could draw his own conclusions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Brotherhood is in the same boat with the Lucifuge and other conspiracies in the time before they became conspiracies. Some of them didn't evolved and than gained Endowments, but first had a supernatural basis which eventually turned into their Endowments when they reached tier 3. The process on which they gained their status as conspiracies was also the one which shaped their powers into the form of Endowments, be it the Rite, Castigations, Elixirs or the Rites of Denial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T01:59:54-08:00","id":27839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=27572#post27572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't have an access to my Witchfinder book right now, so my to access to the exact mechanics of the Rite is limited to my memory.</div> </div> </div> </div> The relevant bit is that the mechanics for the rite are exactly the same at all points in the Compact's history. The only difference was a negative dice-pool modifier that decreased over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/20503-has-anyone-done-work-on-divorcing-the-various-aspects-of-the-tier-system?p=27572#post27572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Rite always worked, but in order to it to become an Endowment the Brotherhood had to decipher the text and understand how it worked in more than &quot;you kill a witch and get her powers&quot;, so they could teach it to anyone who will join the compact.</div> </div> </div> </div> Canonically Jacob could teach it from day one though.<br /> <br /> And &quot;you kill a witch and get her powers&quot; absolutely is an Endowment. It's a supernatural trick that can be easily taught. Understanding the Rite didn't create the Endowment, it was an Endowment from day one. Understanding the Rite just made the Endowment better by removing that dice penalty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:00:37-08:00","id":27877,"title":"","content":"ok, while I don't like binary logic and things like that in order to think about something, I think that doing so is the only way in this case-<br /> a) only conspiracies have Endowments<br /> b) the Promethean Brotherhood had the Rite of Hecate since their beginning<br /> c)it is unknown what makes a supernatural merit into an Endowment<br /> Conclusion- for some reason, the Rite wasn't considered to be an Endowment before the Brotherhood reached the &quot;almost conspiracy&quot; level. The reason is the same reason for why Castigations and Elixirs were not always Endowments.<br /> <br /> As long as no Word of God or other cases in future books will invalid one of those rules, create a new rule or change one of the rules, the conclusion is still valid. This is the only way to keep the &quot;internal logic of the game&quot; in check. If you want to break that logic, feel free to ignore that conclusion. If you don't you must accept the conclusion<br /> <br /> (damn, I sound like the God Machine! Help!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:40:50-08:00","id":27893,"title":"","content":"To me.<br /> <br /> 1) The Promethean Brotherhood had The Rites of Hecate is a nearly identical form as a Cell, Compact and (soon) as a Conspiracy.<br /> 2) The Rites of Hectate are an Endowment.<br /> <br /> 3) Therefore: Not only Conspiracies have Endowments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel that Hunter broke it's own internal logic. No matter what definition of Tier you use (I've seen several) there's at least one group that breaks it. That's why I want to take the Tier concept apart, examine each of the possibilities, and give the Storyteller tools to rebuild it in new and interesting ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T05:33:28-08:00","id":27916,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case I wish you good luck and follow your work. Who knows? Maybe you'll even manage to convince me that you are right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:05:22-08:00","id":27924,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Outside this thread I'm not trying to say &quot;I'm right&quot; but &quot;here's all the many ways you can look at Tier, imagine the possibilities&quot;. I mean, I do genuinely think that there is no way to define Tier that would accurately classify all the cannon groups currently written; but I also think that &quot;the writers made a mistake&quot; is not really an interesting thing to put in my homebrew. &quot;imagine the possibilities&quot; is a very interesting thing to talk about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now I'm working on an Endowment based Tier scheme which, based on their cannon Endowments, puts half the Conspiracies on Tier 2, splits the Compacts between Tier 1 and 2 and would put one Compact (the Wilde Society) as the sole Tier 4. I actually am going to recommend against using it as a primary Tier scheme but it's an interesting one to think about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:44:24-08:00","id":27944,"title":"","content":"well it sounds to me like you are trying to make something in the style of the Chronicler's Guide for Hunter, which is cool :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:24:48-08:00","id":27960,"title":"","content":"Sort of <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> sort of.<br /> <br /> <br /> Slasher was a book about individual monsters (Hunt Club excluded) but it also sneaked in some new Hunter material and a heck of a lot of useful material about the morality on an individual hunter; and how a hunter degrades into a Slasher.<br /> <br /> Cults does the same. It's mostly a book about cool antagonist organisations, but the guidelines on fighting cults will be a pseudo-players guide for being part of a large organisation and the guidelines on building and running cults can also be used as a pseudo-storytellers guide on running hunter organisations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel that there's a lot of potential in this concept, and I mean a LOT. Guidance for how to actually play the hunter organisations as real organisations and really low level enemies are probably the two biggest missing gaps in the setting. A book about cults provides an opportunity to do fill both, as well as fill the setting with lots of one off weird things. I just hope I'm good enough to do it justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/foru